UID:ed99106bfd37cba7@role-environmental-land-use.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260908T163714Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260828
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] DACF Invites Participation in the 2027 Maine 
 Agricultural Trades Show
DESCRIPTION:Home\nSkip to top navigation\nSkip to side navigation\nSkip to
  content\nSkip to footer\nMaine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp
 \n|\nSearch Maine.gov\nDACF Home\n→\nAbout DACF\n→\nNewsroom\n→ News
 \nDACF Invites Participation in the 2027 Maine Agricultural Trades Show\nA
 ugust 28\, 2026\nBusinesses\, organizations\, educators\, and service prov
 iders are encouraged to get involved and shape Maine's annual agricultural
  gathering\nAUGUSTA - The Maine Department of Agriculture\, Conservation a
 nd Forestry (DACF) is inviting businesses\, farms\, agricultural organizat
 ions\, educators\, researchers\, service providers\, and others connected 
 to Maine agriculture\, food systems\, and natural resources to express int
 erest in participating in the 2027 Maine Agricultural Trades Show\, schedu
 led for January 12-14\, 2027.\nThe annual show brings together Maines agri
 cultural community for three days of exhibits\, education\, professional d
 evelopment\, networking\, and conversations about the opportunities and ch
 allenges facing agriculture and food systems.\nDACF is encouraging both re
 turning participants and organizations that have not previously participat
 ed to explore ways to become involved.\nMany Ways to Participate\nThe Agri
 cultural Trades Show offers several ways for businesses and organizations 
 to connect with attendees and contribute to the program\, including:\nExhi
 bit booths\nfor businesses and organizations offering agricultural service
 s\, supplies\, tools\, equipment\, programs\, and resources.\nConference s
 essions\nfor workshops\, annual meetings\, continuing education\, research
  and development updates\, and discussions focused on agriculture\, food s
 ystems\, and natural resources.\nThe Maine Stage\nfeatures approximately 4
 0-minute programs designed for broad audience appeal\, including farmer sp
 otlights\, demonstrations\, interviews\, and other presentations.\nRoom re
 ntals\nfor focus groups\, competitions\, meetings\, and other agriculture-
 focused activities.\nSponsorship opportunities\nsupporting show programmin
 g\, hospitality\, audi\nhttps://www.maine.gov/dacf/about/news/news.shtml?i
 d=13362219
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dacf/about/news/news.shtml?id=13362219
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
